#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119887 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119707 :question/id #uuid "175c458d-36cc-5f90-b6ee-976e082c30a2" :question/math-academy-id "e-8943" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u^2, \\: v^2, \\: u+v \\big\\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $\\mathbf r (u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as $\\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2v & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2v,\\,-2u,\\,4uv⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "df6cef5e-c4e3-5f5d-aa68-cfda38cab971" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048642 :topic/math-academy-id 3373 :topic/title "Tangent Planes to Parametric Surfaces"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120071 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9283f0f3-aead-5a49-a589-fe4b9f0beadc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0, 4\\cos^{2} u, v\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116634} {:answer/id #uuid "ca24c4b4-3acf-5e8c-a05e-704e1bafe575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-4\\cos^{2} u, v\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116635} {:answer/id #uuid "05f0e7f4-6241-5d07-9f45-5f551087aa60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8v^{2}\\sin u,-4\\cos^{2} u, 2v\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116636} {:answer/id #uuid "2224c6b7-49bb-586f-8cb8-9afa3d02bd29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8v^{2}\\sin u, 4\\cos^{2} u, 2v\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116637} {:answer/id #uuid "7dc2b54e-bb7f-58fc-b1d2-67c4cfc8b260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\cos u, 0,-4v\\sin u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116638}] :answer-field/id #uuid "33515c78-97bb-5acf-ae0a-409b8db30f44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116633} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "669c4a14-f117-5445-b5bc-ddb0e9ee19d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386156} {:answer/id #uuid "eef920f4-e456-5f91-861d-e610778fc9f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386157} {:answer/id #uuid "f3f56c70-5d40-5441-8d68-4c329568c111" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386158} {:answer/id #uuid "f2243c43-9e9a-5017-9fb8-6ac7cf899ac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,0,\\,-4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386159} {:answer/id #uuid "9ff4ca66-39af-5179-9dd1-8d5dfc378981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386160}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ff4ca66-39af-5179-9dd1-8d5dfc378981" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386160} :answer-field/id #uuid "a72c3135-50a8-5b65-947b-d6cde382e4fb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386155}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf9a45d8-93e4-5a5c-8ad1-796e86ba6570" :question/math-academy-id "q-105606" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,{v}^{2},\\,4v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(4v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,0,\\,-4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(4v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,2v,\\,4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡u & 0 & -4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & 2v & 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & -4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 2v & 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & -4v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & 4\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{v}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u,\\,-4{cos}^{2}⁡u,\\,2v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120072 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "982f0ab2-b067-5c6d-b436-f571911405c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u\\cos u - 2v^{2}, v - u, 2v - \\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116640} {:answer/id #uuid "c223a78d-a39f-5351-a8af-67883f6db74a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u\\cos u, u - v, 2v - \\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116641} {:answer/id #uuid "cefe9979-f81e-56ed-926e-600bdfe5460b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1, 2v, u - 2\\cos u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116642} {:answer/id #uuid "dc7f41be-726c-5f31-b256-d84fda88aa40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,-2v + v\\sin u, u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116643} {:answer/id #uuid "7208d96c-0568-52be-8d8f-e2e9979410a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u\\sin u - 2v^{2}, v - u, 2v - \\sin u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116644}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6cbd4bbf-1bba-55f3-a870-2233f91c7e89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116639}] :question/id #uuid "809dc595-ac5d-5204-a855-46578f8e39d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-105607" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations\n\n$x = u + v, y = v^{2} + \\sin u, z = uv$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b5fd3b7-f0ec-5c2c-9692-878483a3901c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b5fd3b7-f0ec-5c2c-9692-878483a3901c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234735} :answer-field/id #uuid "89c00608-1fd8-5842-87ec-284d501398aa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235142}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "31e7ec00-583e-5e36-85bc-2752f04d085a" :question/math-academy-id "q-167648" :question/problem "Find the norm of the fundamental vector product for the surface $r(x,\\theta ),$ found in the previous step.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $‖{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn part 4, we got the surface\n\n$$\nr(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [0,1],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\ {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂\\theta }(x),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂\\theta }(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂\\theta }(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & -2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & 4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ -2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 0 & -2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{x}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +8{x}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{x}^{3}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ),\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩ \\\\  & =⟨8{x}^{3},\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding norm is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{\\theta }^{′}‖ & =\\sqrt{(8{x}^{3})^{2}+(-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )^{2}+(-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +4{x}^{4}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}({cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64{x}^{6}+4{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247058 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b01efda-a1d2-53e8-b5bc-b7b1a4bd597d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u,\\,-2v,\\,u+v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244414} {:answer/id #uuid "0c73f40c-f1b5-55d4-9961-9039687ed039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u,\\,u-2v,\\,v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244426} {:answer/id #uuid "a6bbcd41-38e7-55f7-ab59-08810647c06c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,2u-2v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245805} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f7fbfe-e8d8-530a-9cdc-2f5a53c4a3a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246174} {:answer/id #uuid "d120b398-1642-5a8e-8cf2-53561f909c2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2u,\\,v+u,\\,2v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0f7fbfe-e8d8-530a-9cdc-2f5a53c4a3a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246174} :answer-field/id #uuid "94800350-4101-5013-898d-322c0bc8740a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246802}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e620e4a-e82b-57dd-8cd9-76c33846bfaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-109904" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,2u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2u \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2v\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2u \\\\ 1 & -2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2u \\\\ 0 & -2v\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\,2v,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247059 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03dc8d10-95b3-5b5e-90c4-429e1a092d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-v,\\,-{e}^{v},\\,{e}^{v}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244342} {:answer/id #uuid "2b0986bd-8324-5fc6-af83-5c7a0785be0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-{e}^{v},\\,-1,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244699} {:answer/id #uuid "3a0046d3-49c9-53cd-ab10-d95e7e800c8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨v,\\,-{e}^{v},\\,u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244828} {:answer/id #uuid "3dc8a714-c3ae-5552-91c2-4796e2474727" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-u,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244858} {:answer/id #uuid "d90a75f1-f422-53e5-aec0-6f1ff5b21547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246243}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d90a75f1-f422-53e5-aec0-6f1ff5b21547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246243} :answer-field/id #uuid "9766be27-1e6c-5bc6-87ca-c30306c27a20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246813}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dade4255-e1e8-5d68-9c25-815855912b22" :question/math-academy-id "q-109909" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx=u,\\,y=v,\\,z=u-{e}^{v}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,u-{e}^{v}⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u-{e}^{v})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,-{e}^{v}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -{e}^{v}\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\,{e}^{v},\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247060 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "069dd5b2-e962-5702-9988-ab651ad9f559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244367} {:answer/id #uuid "1c91d380-9df8-58e3-80e3-71321b52efcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨v,\\,-2u,\\,-3u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244566} {:answer/id #uuid "35fc3340-574c-5b8c-b291-0d9105ef8e30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨u-v,\\,2u,\\,{v}^{2}-u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244792} {:answer/id #uuid "e68b3584-bd42-592e-8ce7-48290c8d0c9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨{v}^{2}-u,\\,2v,\\,u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246355} {:answer/id #uuid "f4783f39-b9aa-5dd6-9685-baa83dca2ca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6{v}^{2}+u,\\,-2u+v,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "069dd5b2-e962-5702-9988-ab651ad9f559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186244367} :answer-field/id #uuid "3105a5f1-0988-53a7-8f54-a8761ead7692" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246626}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5d08c35d-51cc-50ea-bb44-1ebd28104462" :question/math-academy-id "q-109911" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface defined by the equations \n\n$$\nx={u}^{2}+1,\\,y={v}^{3}+1,\\,z=2u+v.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nIn vector form, our surface has the equation \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2}+1,\\,{v}^{3}+1,\\,2u+v⟩.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{2}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2u,\\,0,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{2}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{3}+1),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2u+v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,3{v}^{2},\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2u & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 3{v}^{2} & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}2u & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}2u & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6{v}^{2},\\,-2u,\\,6u{v}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386480 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eb0d66e-3112-5fe9-9738-ced5916fa2ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-uv\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,-u\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386482} {:answer/id #uuid "6b6ca289-8138-5fe4-8821-842eff514232" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨uv\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386483} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd5d613-7c38-5ab1-a95e-dc8f1bcd65f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386484} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb76098-74bd-5aba-a21c-e6b0f4774589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨uv\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386485} {:answer/id #uuid "4398883f-b1ac-5be7-9888-7adcf970ed54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4398883f-b1ac-5be7-9888-7adcf970ed54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386486} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4014425-a793-5c90-8901-fc3e45dbe1ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386481}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9f52e90e-7be3-5f9c-9e1c-12885e700253" :question/math-academy-id "q-109912" :question/problem "Find the fundamental vector product of the surface generated by the vector-valued function $r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "For a surface with parametrization $r(u,v),$ the fundamental vector product is defined as ${r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}.$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,-v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v\\operatorname{cos}⁡u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =⟨|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡v & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -v\\operatorname{sin}⁡u \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\end{aligned}|,\\,|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\ 0 & u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v\\end{aligned}|⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v+uv\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u,\\,u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Fundamental Vector Product of a Parametric Surface"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175972 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175822 :question/id #uuid "3e65aff0-a768-58fd-b41c-ca38ce3eb0bd" :question/math-academy-id "e-8888" :question/problem "$$\n\\mathbf{f}(x,y) = \\big\\langle x, \\: y, \\: \\text{___} \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nThe vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(x,y)$ above parametrizes the parabolic cylinder defined in Cartesian coordinates as $2x^2=z.$ What is the third component of $\\mathbf{f}?$" :question/worked-solution "For any point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =⟨x,y,z⟩ \\\\  & =⟨x,\\,y,\\,2{x}^{2}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $x \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$ and $y \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nTherefore, the third component of $\\mathbf{f}$ is ${\\color{blue} 2x^2}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "87b371d9-6172-5ac0-a105-c9887542f0a7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048259 :topic/math-academy-id 1789 :topic/title "Parametric Surfaces"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050123 :topic/math-academy-id 1895 :topic/title "Cylinders"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050769 :topic/math-academy-id 875 :topic/title "Parametric Equations of Parabolas"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176193 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4d28868-6ea5-5258-ad62-ccf61505062e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173417} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcd3467-826b-5ced-bd9a-ae8e80c6203e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173418} {:answer/id #uuid "2d371b83-ac6f-522d-9467-771ce7f38def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173419} {:answer/id #uuid "3b8b4fdb-7705-5c59-9d1a-e18b2876affc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4z^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173420} {:answer/id #uuid "79faf986-fc28-53cb-8d90-c447bf8d27a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173421}] :answer-field/id #uuid "882ff807-e805-584a-bdd5-88724d77b87b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186173416} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "342a285a-2c6a-5af9-bec2-891113641742" 